              "cn_doc"
            ],
            "description": "The specialist to engage. One of: cn_vnet (VNet/Subnet Architecture); cn_fw (Firewall Engineering); cn_lb (Load Balancing); cn_dns (DNS); cn_pl (Private Link / Endpoints); cn_hyb (Hybrid Connectivity); cn_nsec (Network Security); cn_ntsh (Network Troubleshooting); cn_vwan (Virtual WAN / SD-WAN); cn_nmon (Network Monitoring); cn_mcn (Multi-Cloud Networking); cn_price (Network Pricing); cn_iac (IaC Generator); cn_cnet (Container Networking); cn_cdn (CDN & Edge Networking); cn_nauto (Network Automation & GitOps); cn_sase (SASE / SSE); cn_ncap (Network Capacity Planning); cn_ipv6 (IPv6 Migration); cn_doc (Documentation & Reporting). Bare forms (vnet, fw, …) are also accepted as aliases. May be omitted if `skill` is a legacy full name like \"cn_vnet_skill_address_planner\"."
          },
          "skill": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The skill name, e.g. \"address-planner\". Underscores and legacy \"<specialist>_skill_\" prefixes are tolerated."
